# ============================================================
# _redirects: Cloudflare Pages. First match wins.
# 301 = permanent (search engines move the ranking across).
#
# DO NOT add "pretty URL" rules like `/about  /about.html`.
# Cloudflare Pages already serves /about.html at /about, and it
# redirects /about.html → /about on its own. A rule pointing the
# other way makes an infinite loop:
#
#     /about → (this file) → /about.html → (Pages) → /about → …
#
# which browsers show as ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS, the page simply
# never loads. That is exactly what a previous version of this
# file did to about, insights, portfolio, colophon, contact,
# tools and learn. Every destination below is therefore
# extensionless, so Pages has nothing left to rewrite.
# ============================================================

# Retired pages that still have links pointing at them.
# Both spellings of the source, because a visitor may arrive at either.
#
# The two admin pages are the React ones now, and the pages they
# replaced are in archive/, out of the deploy, as of 16 August
# 2026. These two lines are what stops a bookmark landing on the
# 404 page. Both destinations end in index.html deliberately: the
# extensionless form would be rewritten by Cloudflare and the note
# at the top of this file is about exactly that loop.
/studio.html          /studio/index.html    301
/desk.html            /desk/index.html      301
/work.html            /portfolio            301
/work                 /portfolio            301
/services.html        /portfolio            301
/services             /portfolio            301
# The colophon described a site with no framework, no build step and
# no dependencies, and every one of those sentences stopped being
# true during the transition (TRANSITION.md, stages 9 to 11). It was
# a page about how the site was built, so it went rather than being
# rewritten into a page about how it used to be built. /about answers
# the question it was answering.
/colophon.html        /about                301
/colophon             /about                301
/insights/dsex.html   /learn/terms/dsex     301
/insights/dsex        /learn/terms/dsex     301

# The three reading hubs, pointing at the canonical address rather
# than away from it (TRANSITION.md Stage 11.1).
#
# This is the one place the warning at the top does not apply, and
# the reason is worth reading before touching it. That warning is
# about Cloudflare rewriting /about.html to /about behind your back,
# so a rule pointing the other way bounces for ever. These three
# addresses are in `run_worker_first` in wrangler.toml, which takes
# them away from the asset router altogether: nothing rewrites them,
# the Next.js Worker answers them, and there is no other side to the
# bounce. `check-routes.mjs` reads that list and models it, so if the
# entry in wrangler.toml is ever removed, these six lines become the
# loop it has always been able to catch.
/about                 /about.html           301
/contact               /contact.html         301
/insights              /insights.html        301
/cooking               /cooking/index.html   301
/cooking/              /cooking/index.html   301
/travel                /travel/index.html    301
/travel/               /travel/index.html    301

# Feed aliases: .xml isn't touched by the HTML handling, so these are safe.
/rss                  /feed.xml             301
/feed                 /feed.xml             301
/sitemap              /sitemap.xml          301
